{
  "title": "A4 - Coding structure",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Backend layers",
      "description": "In feature packages such as funds, the backend follows a router–service–repository structure. This separates how we handle requests, coordinate business rules and access the database.",
      "directory": "backend/src/funds"
    },
    {
      "title": "Router",
      "description": "The router handles the HTTP request and response. Here, it receives the filter parameters and passes them to the service.",
      "file": "backend/src/funds/routes.py",
      "line": 76
    },
    {
      "title": "Service",
      "description": "The service coordinates the business rules, working with the repositories and delegating matching rules to the fund matcher.",
      "file": "backend/src/funds/service.py",
      "line": 28
    },
    {
      "title": "Repository",
      "description": "The repository handles the database queries. Here, it applies the filters, orders the funds by name and executes the query.",
      "file": "backend/src/funds/repository.py",
      "line": 80
    },
    {
      "title": "Frontend responsibilities",
      "description": "On the frontend, we also separate responsibilities. Pages bring the screen together, components provide reusable interface elements, hooks manage state and logic, and services communicate with the backend and Supabase.",
      "directory": "frontend/src"
    },
    {
      "title": "Utilities",
      "description": "Utilities contain smaller, tested functions. This percentage formatter, for example, has tests covering formatting and missing values.",
      "file": "frontend/src/utils/fundsCopy.ts",
      "line": 861
    },
    {
      "title": "Page components",
      "description": "The funds catalogue shows how these layers work together. The page brings together components such as the filters and fund cards.",
      "file": "frontend/src/pages/Funds.tsx",
      "line": 294
    },
    {
      "title": "Filter state",
      "description": "When a user changes a filter, the page updates its state and passes the filters to the catalogue hook.",
      "file": "frontend/src/pages/Funds.tsx",
      "line": 84
    },
    {
      "title": "Catalogue hook",
      "description": "The hook reloads the data when those filters change and manages the loading and error states.",
      "file": "frontend/src/hooks/useFundCatalogue.ts",
      "line": 18
    },
    {
      "title": "API service",
      "description": "It calls this API service, which makes the backend request with the selected filters.",
      "file": "frontend/src/services/api/fundCatalogue.ts",
      "line": 268
    },
    {
      "title": "Results and maintainability",
      "description": "The page then uses that state to show loading, an error, an empty result or the fund cards.\n\nThis separation gives us a consistent way to organise, test and maintain the code.",
      "file": "frontend/src/pages/Funds.tsx",
      "line": 313
    }
  ]
